  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Build a new Neonatal Care Unit, Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HHA&apos;s existing Neonatal Unit opened in 2012, able to treat up to 8 unwell babies. It quickly became stretched beyond capacity, regularly caring for 14 babies at a time who are forced to share cots and oxygen. We have now finalised plans to build a new Neonatal Care Unit, with the capacity to accommodate 16 babies, a breastfeeding/family care room, postnatal ward, chapel, training room, staff offices and accommodation.  This unit will save the lives of thousands of babies in the years to come.</narrative>
  </description>
